WEBVTT

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:14.410
Presently, there are hundreds of alien species coming and going, living their lives on Earth.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.030
Species that come in peace...

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.780
Aggressive, warlike species...

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.890
Species on the brink of extinction...

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.960
All kinds of alien species, from the level of international intrigue,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.800
to individual crimes, to research, with a kaleidoscope of different goals.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.970
They coexist with us, and maintain a precarious balance.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.290
A UFO?

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.600
And the only ones who don't realize this... are us humans!

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:57.650
The towns entrance is adorned with a cow's skull

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:02.610
It's fine that the law is decided by the strongest,

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.600
But this simple feeling will not be enough to fulfill you

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.080
Everyone will definitely revolt and shortly disappear

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.360
That's a shocking bloody picture

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:23.510
I'm feeling nauseous

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:33.720
Holding my head, I board the subway

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:44.160
Righteous way of living, righteous way of dying

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:54.610
Who on earth knows or what the hell can show me?

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:04.800
Cold finger girl

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.950
Sit Down

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:30.890
Yamagata!

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.680
Yamagata!

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.440
Yup, it's still chilly out here.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:44.030
It's not completely because I wanted to keep playing baseball.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.490
But holding the title for best middle school baseball team in Japan isn't just for show.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.660
All-star Baseball Tournament

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.660
Aim for the National Championship

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:54.330
Even a perpetual benchwarmer like myself gets talked about after being recommended for admission.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.460
In other words, I was drafted to play baseball at this school.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.770
The third pitch... it's thrown... and he hits it!

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.680
All I actually wanted was to move out on my own,

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.800
Hit center left, one bounce, two bounce, it's a hit!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.780
so I jumped at the chance to use this as a pretext.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:13.020
Runner from first hits second, heads right onto third,

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.070
the center fielder turns, catches the ball, and just throws it back to second!

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.140
You from Tokyo?

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.540
Uh, y-yeah.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.620
One out, runners on first and third!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.380
I'll be attending high school here starting this year.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.240
Kisaragi High School?

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.570
How'd you know?

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:29.120
Their baseball team's been scoutin' out good players recently.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.040
Work hard.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.290
You get popular and you'll be rakin' in the girlies!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.560
Oh, come on!

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.750
I was totally unpopular back in middle school!

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:44.170
Oh, but with your fresh young Tokyo smile, you won't be able to keep 'em off ya!

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.820
Whoa, look at all the calluses ya got!

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.280
Best in Japan... A class of its own.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.310
People are bigger baseball fans than I expected.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.820
Um, about my room...

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.320
Ah! Sorry about that!

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.420
Here's your key!

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.690
This is the place.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.360
Wow, what an awesome view!

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.320
Starting today, huh...

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.370
They're open?

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.780
My mom?

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.750
Why'd she have to butt in...

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:04.980
Mom!

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.170
Who are you?

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.140
That's <i>my</i> line.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:34.680
Why are you...

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.460
...and those are my clothes!

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.880
Were you the one who unpacked my stuff?

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.140
It was quite a job.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.840
Your desk was pretty heavy.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.780
I didn't ask for your help!

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.960
How the hell did you get in here?

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:48.780
This is the 5th floor!

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.370
Are you some kinda ex-gymnast burgler bastard?!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.380
Burgler?

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.680
No, no...

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.800
I am an alien.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.520
WE ARE ALIENS.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.150
It seems like my spaceship crash landed.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.960
I get it, must be the springtime.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.100
These kind of characters come out of the woodwork.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.660
Enough of this. Get out.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.970
Huh, what?

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.480
Could you please speak more slowly, and clearly?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.670
I am not yet accustomed to this planet's language.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.590
I said GET OUT!!

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.700
Wait, we haven't finished speaking yet.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.710
Bug me again and I'll call the police!

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:28.760
Damn it!

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.510
DON'T OPEN IT!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.440
Jesus! Creepin' me out.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:37.680
I'll eat something and clear...

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.700
Now look here, you!

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:44.300
Will you please at least listen to what I have to say?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:50.020
Are you aware that an unidentified object crash-landed nearby the night before last?

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.440
Oh, that? Didn't they say it was a meteor or something?

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.230
It was a small escape pod.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.110
I was on board, and then came here.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:58.750
It was even on the news.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:06:59.500
Here's a spoon.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:00.460
Thank you.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.910
...and this is <i>my</i> apartment!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:07.110
You sure complain a lot despite my explaining all this to you.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:09.050
It's too strong.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:09.920
Choke on it!

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.590
So, unfortunately, we reporters cannot get any closer.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:18.940
However we have received footage of the crashed object thought to be a meteorite.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:19.960
Take a look.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:24.080
We received this footage from someone on scene, and we apologize for it being blurry,

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:30.100
but inside this giant seed-like object, you can definitely see what looks to be instruments and a cockpit!

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.980
For real?

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:35.940
This object was surely created by intelligent life!

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.420
See?

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:41.410
Even if that's the case, you have no proof that you were inside that thing.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:45.510
You're wearing <i>my</i> clothes, and your body looks identical to a human's.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:49.300
If you're really an alien, show me some damn proof!

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.130
I said <i>proof</i>!

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:54.840
What are we now, 12?

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.630
You're one to talk, asshole!

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.590
I apologize, but I don't have any proof!

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.350
It seems the shock from the crash landing made me to lose my memories.

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.100
All I have...

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:06.550
What's this?

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:09.840
I don't know, but I was gripping it when I regained consciousness.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:11.830
Some kind of controller?

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:13.980
Huh?

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.910
Something terrible has happened!

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.920
The UFO has just exploded in a huge blast!

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.940
It's difficult to tell from here,

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.830
but we're looking at a great number of people that were surely caught up in the explosion!

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:30.380
No way...

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:33.410
Perhaps that was a self-destruct switch?

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:34.100
Wait...

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.910
I bet people died in that explosion, don't you think?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.410
The SDF, protecting the peace of Japan...

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.580
The scientists, slaving day and night in the pursuit of progress...

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.970
In just such an instant, their precious lives turned to naught but ash!

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:48.240
Each one with their own family...

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.980
Some perhaps newlyweds starting a family...

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.120
Clinging to a bundle of tiny new life...

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.360
The anger with no one to direct it towards...

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.700
The unrelenting sadness...

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.340
Those that remain must carry it with them for the rest of their lives!

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.490
They think, everyday...

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.510
If it weren't for that explosion...

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.130
And it's all your fault.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.390
It was a coincidence!

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.960
The explosion just happened to be at the same time I moved that switch, that's all...

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.760
You seriously believe that was a coincidence?!

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.360
You hypocrite!

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:23.380
This is all because you broke into here in the first place!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:24.510
Oh, passing the blame are we?

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.650
That was quick of you.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.180
No way, are they already...

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.960
I'm Edogawa Miho, and I just moved next door.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:37.380
I know this isn't much, but...

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.310
She's cute!

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:41.910
I'm Tsutsui Yukitaka.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:43.660
You really didn't have to go to the trouble.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.880
I just moved here myself.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:46.560
Right.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.300
The landlord mentioned you, the future star.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.320
Baseball, was it?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.540
Yeah, that's the one.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:54.420
You live by yourself?

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:55.000
Yup.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.260
I moved here because of my father's work,

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:05.040
but since he's always staying at the research lab, it's the same as living alone.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.250
Research?

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.020
Yes!

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:08.010
He's a professor of engineering.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.170
Right now he's at the scene of the UFO crash everyone's talking about.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:13.700
Is something wrong?

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:16.280
But... didn't it just explode?

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.320
Oh, don't worry about that.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.610
He called me afterwards.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.440
Oh... Phew.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.460
Well, I need to unpack.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:25.220
See you later.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:26.610
S-Sure.

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:31.240
If you have anything heavy you need help with...

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:32.990
Thank you!

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:35.280
I hope we're in the same class.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.590
Kisaragi High School.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:46.390
Edogawa Miho-chan, huh?

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.620
My high school life's gettin' off to a good start!

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.050
But before that...

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:03.840
I hit the self-destruct switch and killed lotsa people!

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:04.890
Ding-dong...

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.640
How do you do? Fufu...

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.510
I'm Edogawa Miho!

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:11.020
Howdy there, nicetameetcha.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.750
Papa's a scientist and went to investigate the UFO!

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:16.180
What? But it 'sploded! He okay?

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.820
He called, so AOK!

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.130
Thank goodness!

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.800
You have the makings of an excellent psychopathic killer.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.060
That's enough. Get out.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.640
I have no place to go.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:35.730
Please let me stay here for a while.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:36.540
I refuse!

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.850
Please... I'm begging you.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.730
Absolutely, positively, no way!

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:40.850
I see...

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.590
Then, I have no other choice.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.480
Next, I need to...

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:51.310
The true culprit behind the UFO explosion!!

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:50.420
Ah, ah! Attention passersby!

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:50.420
Up there... Isn't that Tsutsui-kun's...?

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.450
S-Stop it!

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:53.670
When did he...

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.180
Taking it isn't going to help.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.830
I've prepared a great many.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:56.830
Why, you...

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:00.500
Just for today.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:04.140
Or so he thinks. As long as I have a way to threaten him I'm bunking here.

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.740
Put that away!

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:08.010
It escaped from somewhere?

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.490
Why do you think that?

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.640
Because there aren't any wild ones near here.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:13.830
I see.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:31.530
Prior to the conclusion of the investigation, I cannot say anything more.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:33.540
Conan Research Laboratory

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:33.540
Professor of Engineering Edogawa Ranzo

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:34.240
But can we take this as confirmation of the existence of alien life?

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:36.210
But, can we take this as confirmation of the existence of alien life?

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:36.810
So that's Miho-chan's dad...

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:39.580
Like I said, I cannot say anything more.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:41.360
If you were going to buy some for me too, you should have said so.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.650
I prefer salt flavour when it comes to instant noodles.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.340
Shut up and eat!

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:47.010
We have breaking news.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:50.570
In regards to the recent explosion, thankfully there were no people close by,

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:53.190
and we have confirmed there were no fatalities.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.370
Let me repeat.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.900
We have confirmed there were zero fatalities.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.040
You hear that?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.200
Just so you know, I don't like the freeze-dried noodle variety.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:01.570
Don't play dumb!

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.830
Did you see that? They said there weren't any fatalities!

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:06.560
Now you don't have anything to threaten me about.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:11.700
It doesn't change the fact that you blew up the UFO... thinks the alien.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:13.410
Then go and say it.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.990
Think about it.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:20.180
No one is gonna believe anything a guy like you says!

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:21.170
You wanna say it? Go on.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.890
Here. Take it.

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:26.430
Indeed...

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.380
It is exactly as you say.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:31.500
I apologize.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.800
What? You mad?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:37.490
Not really.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.860
Where are you going?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:41.970
I am leaving.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.110
Oh, yes...

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.190
Can I have these clothes and shoes, at least?

00:13:48.190 --> 00:13:49.750
I really have nothing else to wear.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:53.080
Sure, fine.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:53.980
Thank you.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:55.680
Goodbye.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:13:57.870
Wait.

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.340
Sheesh... Until tomorrow.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.010
Thank you.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.790
Why'd he get meek all of a sudden?

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:24.180
This!

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.550
You... When did...

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.040
I have to take it back!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.290
This is a sketch of the object we created from witness testimony.

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:34.120
What do you think it is?

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.300
I can't tell for certain,

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:40.450
but I believe it to be extraterrestrial in origin.

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:41.470
They look similar...

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.260
What are you...

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:49.350
I'm going to get it back.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.540
Hey!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.980
Completely fine after jumping from this height?

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:05.700
He's...

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:08.140
He's actually a real...

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:13.220
That idiot!

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.680
Is he retarded?

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.610
If he's so athletic he should've been able to dodge a damn car!

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.290
Crap!

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:27.510
If he's really an alien, and carried to some hospital and examined...

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:33.310
Yukitaka.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.080
Blue blood...

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.180
See? I told you to rest at my place.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:49.270
No...

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.880
I cannot contaminate your place.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:53.220
And besides...

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.540
Besides what?

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:56.830
This will be fine.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.010
Are you...

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:12.310
I'm sorry.

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:14.180
Let me rest a little.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.500
There's no mistaking it anymore.

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:03.550
This guy's an honest to goodness alien!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.440
Somewhere in the Prefecture

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:08.440
Conan Research Laboratory

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:16.310
T-This is...

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:25.050
Hey, sorry, but I have morning practice starting today...

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:31.070
He's...

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.920
What's wrong, best middle school in Japan?

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.530
Let her fly forward! Forward!

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:43.370
Right!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.050
Bring it!

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:52.720
Getting a new recruit to do this even before the entrance ceremony...

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.510
This school's baseball team is serious business.

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.630
Already getting hazed, I see.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.570
Oh, good morning.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:01.420
Jogging?

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.220
Yup! 10 kilometers every day.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:06.230
I no longer need to make my father's lunches, so...

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:09.090
Oh, yeah. I saw your dad on TV yesterday.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.670
Yeah...

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:16.850
He was hiding something.

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:18.600
I can tell.

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:20.040
Really?

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:25.310
I called Conan Laboratory yesterday, but he said he was busy and hung up.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.710
I guess he doesn't trust me after all...

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:33.360
Oh, sorry for bothering you when you're busy.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:34.790
Later!

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:35.780
I'm sure...

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.400
I'm sure he just didn't want to worry you.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.360
He'll tell you about it if you give him time.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:48.580
Yeah!

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.590
Well, whatever.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.300
We're from Conan Police Station.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:12.600
We have word that a criminal has escaped to this area.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:14.210
Can you take a look at this?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:16.870
This is the man.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.450
Nope, haven't seen 'im.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.680
Ah, I see.

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:23.120
If you'll excuse us.

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:26.290
Uh... What did he do?

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:29.460
He's a murderer.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.960
A murderer? Him?

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.480
Oh, what a marvelous performance!

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:46.730
You are truly a gifted criminal!

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:48.820
I don't wanna hear that from you!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:50.210
Have a dango?

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:52.200
I just can't get accustomed to sweet beans...

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:54.150
Whatever!

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:56.180
So... Did you really do it?

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:56.780
Do what?

00:19:57.460 --> 00:20:00.330
I heard... that you've killed people.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.830
The one that was almost killed was me.

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:08.790
Kapow.

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.420
You were shot?

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:13.210
Well, I had no choice.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:16.180
I was being a bit aggressive myself.

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:19.980
That's the thing that was on TV yesterday.

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:24.580
I suspect those people were actually from the laboratory, searching for this.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.450
What... is that?

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.460
It will display my true self.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:32.950
The shock from being shot caused me to remember.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:35.820
My true self is displayed inside.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:41.200
But seeing it may cause you quite a bit of unpleasantness.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.580
Will you look, even knowing this?

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:47.430
What about you?

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:48.670
I don't know...

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:51.150
But I feel like I want to show you.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.440
For you...

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.210
Alright.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.260
So, this is what you really look like?

00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.740
Looks the same as you do now.

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:23.840
No. This is not yet my true self.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.180
You've got to be kidding me...

00:21:58.090 --> 00:22:00.760
A fluidic organism from the planet Jacqueline Ess.

00:22:01.070 --> 00:22:02.810
Its name is Clive.

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:06.170
It has an incredibly vast ability to mimic things.

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:10.750
So this is your true self?

00:22:12.150 --> 00:22:15.370
Do you also think it is hideous?

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:27.700
Are you ready?

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:38.210
Do not fear 'The Now' searching for something that can't be seen across this infinite distance

00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:52.430
Under the hundred million glittering lights, I found you searching for your dream

00:22:52.430 --> 00:23:01.190
An infinite world filled with glass shards

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:13.250
Growing up I felt I knew many meaningless things

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:20.710
Shining like a jewel, you soar in the sky, no past, no future

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:26.050
The answer is beyond the sky

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:36.560
Do not fear 'The Dream', in a distant
place where truth and lies are unseen

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:52.290
Under the hundred million glittering lights, flowers sway in the wind

00:23:57.360 --> 00:24:00.280
I'm leaving. I don't want to bother you anymore...

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:01.250
You shouldn't be picking fights, Captain.

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:05.720
But all the blokes from my planet are hotheads...

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:08.430
If they have orders to kill him, he's a goner if they find him.

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:09.740
If something were to happen, there'd be no stopping it, I suspect.

00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:11.170
That's enough fooling around!

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:12.080
Go up against him, and you'll be crushed.

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:13.520
Could he be an alien?

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:15.280
No, just an ordinary person.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:20.890
Next

00:24:16.610 --> 00:24:19.220
Next time: Run after the man.

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:20.890
You got a girl you like?
